<title>ITALY: Olivetti denies plan to sell Omnitel stake.</title>
<headline>Olivetti denies plan to sell Omnitel stake.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian information technology group Olivetti strongly denied a newspaper report it was considering cutting its stake in mobile phone consortium Omnitel.</p>
<p>Olivetti said in a statement it &quot;categorically denied any theory of this nature.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;The investment in Omnitel is, for Olivetti, a strategic fact and there will be no type of downsizing,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The report in Il Sole 24 Ore financial daily had said Olivetti was considering reducing its stake, currently a controlling one of around 35 percent, to ease its 2.7 trillion lire debts.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
